      "content": "The segregationists of that era often relied on deeply ingrained, pseudoscientific ideas about racial hierarchy. They frequently argued for inherent differences in intelligence and moral capacity between races, claiming that mixing races would lead to societal decay. Furthermore, they used the concept of \"separate but equal,\" which was a legal justification to maintain white supremacy under the guise of protecting different communities. These arguments were rooted in a belief system that deemed white superiority natural and necessary for social order.",
